  "claim": "Jean-François André Clervoy was the astronaut for the group that built Olympus-1 who participated in missions with European Space Agency. An astronaut on Expedition 14 did not.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: Jean-François André Clervoy (born 19 November 1958) is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\nPage: Jean-François Clervoy. Sentence: He is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\nPage: Thomas Reiter. Sentence: Thomas Arthur Reiter (born 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany) is a retired European astronaut and is a Brigadier General in the German Air Force currently working as ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at the European Space Agency (ESA).\nPage: Expedition 14. Sentence: They joined Thomas Reiter, who had arrived at the ISS on 6 July 2006 aboard Space Shuttle \"Discovery\" during mission STS-121.\nPage: Olympus-1. Sentence: Olympus-1 was a communications satellite built by British Aerospace for the European Space Agency.",
