        "original_id": "ac3fa888-7f3f-561d-9505-8737cc1c562c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jean-François Clervoy, Thomas Reiter\n- Organizations: CNES, ESA, NASA, German Air Force\n- Missions: NASA Space Shuttle missions, STS-121, Expedition 14\n- Places: Frankfurt, West Germany, ISS\n- Products: Olympus-1, Space Shuttle Discovery\n- Companies: British Aerospace\n\nFacts:\n- Jean-François Clervoy was born on 19 November 1958.\n- Thomas Reiter was born on 23 May 1958 in Frankfurt, West Germany.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a French engineer and a CNES and ESA astronaut.\n- Jean-François Clervoy is a veteran of three NASA Space Shuttle missions.\n- Olympus-1 was a communications satellite built by British Aerospace for ESA.\n- On 6 July 2006, Thomas Reiter arrived at the ISS aboard Space Shuttle Discovery during mission STS-121.\n- During Expedition 14, they joined Thomas Reiter at the ISS.\n- Thomas Reiter is a retired European astronaut, a Brigadier General in the German Air Force, and an ESA Interagency Coordinator and Advisor to the Director General at ESA.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
